        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-05 10:07:53.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-10499 pcc: DIO attach copy for encrypted files",
        "message": "LU-10499 pcc: DIO attach copy for encrypted files\n\nThe PCC copy of an encrypted file holds its ciphertext, so the\nkernel copy sets S_PCCCOPY to read the Lustre file as if the key\nwere not loaded.  The DIO copy by ll_fid_path_copy was not used for\nencrypted files, since its direct reads would decrypt the data when\nthe key is loaded.\n\nNow that direct IO of a file opened with O_CIPHERTEXT transfers the\nciphertext whether the key is loaded or not, have ll_fid_path_copy\nopen the source file with O_CIPHERTEXT for its direct IO, and use\nthe DIO copy for encrypted files.  O_CIPHERTEXT has no effect on\nthe direct IO of other files, except that its O_NONBLOCK does not\nrestore a released file, whose copy then fails and the kernel falls\nback to the buffered copy.  A ciphertext read reaches the end of the\nlast encryption unit, so the copy may be up to one unit larger than\nthe clear text size, as with the kernel copy, and the helper and the\nkernel check of the copied size both accept that.\n\nAdd sanity-pcc test_50d to verify the PCC copy of an encrypted file.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-pcc\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-pcc clientarch=aarch64 clientdistro=rocky9.8\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ia3d6809c5e9631d7f375d51d9946fdb3373ebbe5\n"
      },
